WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.940 --> 00:00:04.000
Okay I was raised up on Old Spanish Trail.

2
00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:07.160
Okay.

3
00:00:07.160 --> 00:00:10.420
I'm trying to think of that street.

4
00:00:10.420 --> 00:00:13.600
But it's Old Spanish Trail and Moss Avenue.

5
00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:18.060
Or right now they call it East Burton.

6
00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:19.980
East Burton.

7
00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:27.140
On the corner of East Burton and Moss Avenue, which is Old Spanish Trail.

8
00:00:27.140 --> 00:00:32.720
Maybe a half a mile from here on the left.

9
00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:33.960
I was raised there.

10
00:00:33.960 --> 00:00:37.960
And we used to play down here.

11
00:00:37.960 --> 00:00:39.880
Swim a lot in the pool.

12
00:00:39.880 --> 00:00:43.360
Every Sunday . . . Well every weekend.

13
00:00:43.360 --> 00:00:45.620
In the summertime every day.

14
00:00:45.620 --> 00:00:46.820
Yeah.

15
00:00:46.820 --> 00:00:49.240
This place be full.

16
00:00:49.240 --> 00:00:55.900
Every day playing ball, swimming, just doing whatever.

17
00:00:55.900 --> 00:00:57.420
Every year.

18
00:00:57.420 --> 00:01:02.600
Mossville was an active town for a long time.

19
00:01:02.600 --> 00:01:15.340
Until the late sixties . . . Okay, I was a part of the last graduating class of Mossville.

20
00:01:15.340 --> 00:01:16.100
In ‘69?

21
00:01:16.100 --> 00:01:18.220
In ‘69.

22
00:01:18.220 --> 00:01:31.220
So ‘69, and ‘70, things started getting quiet when they split the community up.

23
00:01:31.220 --> 00:01:34.860
Some students had to go to Sulphur, some had to go to Westlake.

24
00:01:34.860 --> 00:01:40.840
And from that I guess the community just got . . . How you say that?

25
00:01:40.840 --> 00:01:41.760
Disoriented?

26
00:01:41.760 --> 00:01:50.040
And everybody just started losing what they had, what this place had.

27
00:01:50.040 --> 00:01:52.000
And you know we had a lot.

28
00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:57.760
We had a good sports program.

29
00:01:57.760 --> 00:02:01.280
The band was good.

30
00:02:01.280 --> 00:02:04.580
I mean you were just a close community.

31
00:02:04.580 --> 00:02:10.540
See, that pool was here before Mossville High was built.

32
00:02:10.540 --> 00:02:17.040
So it was a guy named Mr. Phillip Broussard I think his name was.

33
00:02:17.040 --> 00:02:23.000
But he'd come every summer and he'll have swimming classes.

34
00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:30.320
And I learned how to swim, I was between seven and eight years old.

35
00:02:30.320 --> 00:02:34.100
Everybody in Mossville my age, we had to learn how to swim.

36
00:02:34.100 --> 00:02:34.880
That was the thing.

37
00:02:34.880 --> 00:02:35.780
Yeah.

38
00:02:35.780 --> 00:02:40.760
So when one learned how, everybody else wanted to learn.

39
00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:46.500
This really was our hangout right here, in the pool.

40
00:02:46.500 --> 00:02:49.440
That's the furthest we went.

41
00:02:49.440 --> 00:02:52.020
Baseball stadium . . . They had a big field over there.

42
00:02:52.020 --> 00:02:59.880
Sometimes the teams go play in Westlake, some would go play in Lake Charles.

43
00:02:59.880 --> 00:03:02.500
But we had good teams.

44
00:03:02.500 --> 00:03:04.740
I mean, Mossville was full.

45
00:03:04.740 --> 00:03:06.520
It was full of children back then.

46
00:03:06.520 --> 00:03:07.240
Full of children.

47
00:03:07.240 --> 00:03:11.600
I mean we just . . . I just enjoyed living here.
